#!/usr/bin/env bash

cat <<'GUIDE'
=== Jar's NixOS Install Guide ===

TARGET DRIVE:
  lsblk                    # find your disk (e.g. /dev/sda, /dev/nvme0n1)

====== PARTITIONING ======

UEFI (modern, default):
  cfdisk /dev/sdX
  - 512M      -> type "EFI System"          -> /boot
  - remaining -> type "Linux filesystem"     -> /

UEFI + separate /home:
  cfdisk /dev/sdX
  - 512M      -> type "EFI System"          -> /boot
  - 50-100G   -> type "Linux filesystem"    -> /
  - remaining -> type "Linux filesystem"    -> /home

UEFI + /home + swap:
  cfdisk /dev/sdX
  - 512M      -> type "EFI System"          -> /boot
  - 50-100G   -> type "Linux filesystem"    -> /
  - 8-32G     -> type "Linux swap"          -> swap
  - remaining -> type "Linux filesystem"    -> /home

Legacy/BIOS:
  cfdisk /dev/sdX
  - 1M        -> type "BIOS boot"           -> (unformatted)
  - remaining -> type "Linux filesystem"    -> /

====== FORMATTING ======

EFI partition (always fat32):
  mkfs.fat -F 32 /dev/sdX1

Root / Home (pick one):
  ext4:  mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdX2
  btrfs: mkfs.btrfs /dev/sdX2
  xfs:   mkfs.xfs /dev/sdX2

  (for separate /home, format /dev/sdX3 the same way)

Swap:
  mkswap /dev/sdX?   &&   swapon /dev/sdX?

====== MOUNTING ======

UEFI basic:
  mount /dev/sdX2 /mnt
  mount --mkdir /dev/sdX1 /mnt/boot

UEFI + separate /home:
  mount /dev/sdX2 /mnt
  mount --mkdir /dev/sdX1 /mnt/boot
  mount --mkdir /dev/sdX3 /mnt/home

btrfs WITH subvolumes (NixOS-safe, optional):
  mount /dev/sdX2 /mnt
  btrfs subvolume create /mnt/@
  btrfs subvolume create /mnt/@home
  btrfs subvolume create /mnt/@nix
  umount /mnt
  mount -o subvol=@     /dev/sdX2 /mnt
  mount --mkdir -o subvol=@home /dev/sdX2 /mnt/home
  mount --mkdir -o subvol=@nix  /dev/sdX2 /mnt/nix
  mount --mkdir /dev/sdX1 /mnt/boot

Verify mounts:  lsblk

====== NETWORK ======

Ethernet usually works out of the box.
Wi-Fi (iwd):
  iwctl
  > station list
  > station wlan0 connect "SSID"

Test:  ping 1.1.1.1

====== CORE INSTALL (what nixinstall does for you) ======

  nixos-generate-config --root /mnt
  nano /mnt/etc/nixos/configuration.nix
    # minimal config: import ./hardware-configuration.nix, bootloader,
    # networkmanager, your user (wheel + password), flakes enabled
  nixos-install --root /mnt --no-root-passwd
  git clone https://github.com/y-jar/nix-config /mnt/home/USER/nix-config
  chown -R USER: /mnt/home/USER

====== REBOOT ======

  umount -R /mnt
  reboot

====== POST-INSTALL (the switch) ======

After reboot, on the new system:
  cd ~/nix-config
  nix-shell
  hardto YOURHOST     # scaffold host + yoink hardware config
  nhs YOURHOST        # deploy (this is the switch)

  HOSTNAME options:
    calender  - main pc
    candle    - gaming mini pc
    loom      - general pc
    vmjar     - virtual machine
    whale     - server
    yilyonix  - test bench
    ziiemar   - laptop

===== INTERACTIVE INSTALLER =====
For a guided experience (does all of the above), run:
  nixinstall
Then pick: Iso Install  (live ISO only, erases disk)
GUIDE
